# Game-app UI surface budget

- **Scope:** Player **game app** UI only (`app/` / `colonizethis_app`): panels, dialogs, overlays, bottom sheets, in-game feature routes, Yarn/Jenny hosts, in-panel minimaps. **Not** `ctdev/`, `tool/`, or `widgetbook_host/` (Widgetbook must still dispose any `FlameGame` it creates). Distinct from the 15-second next-turn budget.
- **Hard usability limit:** From the open trigger until **ready state** (below) must complete in **<= 1,000 ms** (`kUiSurfaceOpenBudgetMs`) on the project target environment. Chrome-only first paint does **not** meet the budget if required content is still loading. Overflows are release-blocking defects for surfaces **introduced or modified** by the work under review.
- **Ready state:** **Start:** user open trigger (tap, route push, tab selection that shows the surface). **End:** first frame after all **required first-open content** (per screen spec or TDD default checklist in `SPEC/program/ui-surface-budget.md`) is visible and interactive — projections applied, minimap/tile layers rendered, Yarn host ready if dialogue is shown, required assets decoded, async loads for mandatory content complete (or deterministic error/placeholder per screen spec). **Excluded:** lazy/off-screen inactive-tab content unless the surface is on the first-open tab allowlist in `SPEC/program/ui-surface-budget.md`.
- **Inactive tabs:** Not in the first-open segment unless the surface is on that allowlist. Selecting a tab starts a new 1,000 ms segment for that tab's required content.
- **Existing overflows:** Surfaces that already exceed 1,000 ms before this policy lands are **grandfathered** for unrelated verification — track them as separate performance defects. The standing verify/accept gate hard-fails only when the issue under review **touches or introduces** a surface whose open path exceeds the budget.
- **Create on show:** Do not construct unused dialogs, panels, overlay widgets, `GameWidget` / `FlameGame`, Jenny runners, or dual-region / full-game view data. Prefer `showDialog` / route push / `if (visible)` over `Offstage`, eager `IndexedStack` of maps, or hidden `OverlayEntry`. Shell dialog registries are factories, not prebuilt widgets. One live `FlameGame` per visible map canvas; no dummy game when the map is absent.
- **Dispose on hide:** Popping or closing a surface must unmount its subtree (`dispose()` / Flame `onRemove()` / cancel subscriptions). Closed UI must not retain a `Game`, `FlameGame`, Jenny runner, or decoded images — especially on mobile.
- **No functional drift:** Staying under budget must not skip SPEC-required content; finish the required load inside 1,000 ms.
- **Standing gate:** `verify-github-issue` and `accept-github-issue` apply this contract to game-app UI work **even when the issue ACs omit it**, scoped to surfaces **introduced or modified** by that issue. Measurement, tests, and ACs: `SPEC/program/ui-surface-budget.md`.
